  "title": "Understanding Verb Patterns",
  "short_title": "Verb patterns",
  "description": "Learn the patterns that make French verbs predictable",
  "can_do": [
    "Expect the {je}, {tu}, {il} and {elle} forms of a verb to sound alike.",
    "Expect -ons for {nous}, -ez for {vous} and a silent -ent for {ils} and {elles}.",
    "Spot {être}, {avoir} and {aller} as the verbs that break these patterns."
  ],
  "minutes": 6,
  "line": "How the verbs you know sound alike, and the three that break the pattern.",
  "parts": [
    {
      "id": "p-french-verbs-follow-patterns",
      "heading": "French verbs follow patterns",
      "text": [
        "French verbs belong to groups, and verbs in a group change in similar ways. Once you hear a pattern, each new verb is easier to learn.",
        "You learned each verb as it is written. This guide is about how the forms sound."
      ]
    },
    {
