    {
      "id": "p-etre-avoir-and-aller",
      "heading": "être, avoir and aller go their own way",
      "text": [
        "Some verbs are used so often that they kept forms of their own. These are the irregular verbs, and you use them so much that they stick. English does the same with am, are and is."
      ],
      "note": "Listen again: {tu} and {il} still sound the same in each of the three.",
